{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And also [these].</b> There are from the people of Judah." "<b>Priest.</b> For he is the one who teaches, and likewise the prophet, he is the one who reproves." "<b>They err in vision.</b> In the words of the seer, the reprovers of the people." "<b>They stumble in judgment.</b> The judges. Now פקו is a verb in active voice, or the word דברי is elided, and this is the correct interpretation, and it is a verb standing alone, from the root ופיק ברכים (Nahum 2:11), in the sense of dislocating the knees."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:32.600170287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}